                <pb facs="0276" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.73/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-22T18:00:00-04:16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 23,
                            1.05 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President signed this afternoon the contract for the laying of the cable from
                    Argentina to Uruguay authorized by the concession granted the Central and South
                    America Telegraph Company August 1, 1918.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
